{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And you shall be to Me a kingdom of priests, etc.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'you shall be to Me' — as My portion. And He called them kings and priests, and He called them as well גוי קדוש — a holy nation — in the receiving of the Torah. And the verse explains to you that in the crown of Torah there are included the crown of priesthood and the crown of kingship; and so our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (Proverbs 3:15): ״יקרה היא מפנינים״ — 'she is more precious than pearls' — more than the High Priest who enters within the innermost sanctuary." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ממלכת כהנים — a kingdom of servants (משרתים), that you shall serve Me in this world; וגוי קדוש — for the world to come. For the word גוי is attached, meaning: a nation of (של) the Holy One — He is the holy Elohim, sanctified through righteousness; and like it (Isaiah 26:2): ״ובא גוי צדיק״ — 'and a righteous nation enters' — a nation of (של) the Righteous One. And so they are assured in this world and in the world to come."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:04.455051960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}